    "correctChoice": "C",
    "explanation": "Conditions that shift the hemoglobin-oxygen dissociation curve\nto the RIGHT (reduced Hgb affinity for oxygen):\n• Exercise\n• Decreased pH\n• Increase in PCO\n2\n• Increased temperature/fever\n• Hypoxia\n• Increased 2,3 DPG\nConditions that shift the hemoglobin-oxygen dissociation curve\nto the LEFT (increased Hgb affinity for oxygen):\n• Increased pH\n• Decreased temperature\n• Presence of fetal Hgb (higher O2 affinity)\n• Decreased 2,3 DPG\n• Increased carbon monoxide and methemoglobin",
