    "explanation": "Adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH), melanocyte-stimulating\nhormone (MSH), beta-lipotropin, and beta-endorphin are\nderived from the precursor molecule proopiomelanocortin\n(POMC).\nThyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH), follicle-stimulating\nhormone (FSH), and luteinizing hormone (LH) have the same\nalpha subunits because they belong to the same glycoprotein\nfamily, but they have different beta subunits which accounts\nfor the unique biological activity of each of them.",
