    "explanation": "Basal electric frequency (slow waves) originate in\nthe interstitial cells of Cajal.\nThe frequency of slow waves varies along the GI tract, the\nhighest being in the duodenum (12 per minute) and the lowest\nbeing in the stomach (3 per minute)\nSome points to remember about slow waves:\n• They set the maximum frequency of contractions for\neach part of the GI tract\n• Not influenced by neural or hormonal input\n• The action potential frequency on top of slow waves is\nmodified by neural and hormonal input.\nRemember the frequency of slow waves:\n“DIS is so slow!”\nDuodenum > Ileum > Stomach",
