    "explanation": "Schwann cells produce myelin for axons in the PNS\n(including CN III-XII). These cells are affected in Guillain-Barré\nsyndrome.\nOligodendrocytes, on the other hand, are the cells\nresponsible for myelinating axons in the CNS (including CN II)\nMicroglia serve as phagocytic scavenger cells of the CNS.\nDerived from mesoderm.\nAstrocytes are the largest and most abundant glial cells in the\nCNS. They provide:\n• Physical support\n• Repair functions\n• Removal of excess neurotransmitters\n• Component of the blood-brain",
