    "correctChoice": "A",
    "explanation": "The period of isovolumetric contraction occurs between the\nclosing of the mitral valve and the opening of the aortic\nvalve, representing the phase with the highest oxygen\nconsumption.\nPhases of the cardiac cycle of the left ventricle\n1. Isovolumetric contraction occurs between the\nclosing of the mitral valve and the opening of the aortic\nvalve, representing the phase with the highest\noxygen consumption.\n2. Systolic ejection is the period from aortic valve\nopening to closing.\n3. Isovolumetric relaxation takes place between aortic\nvalve closing and mitral valve opening.\n4. Rapid filling characterizes the phase just after the\nmitral valve opens.\n5. Reduced filling corresponds to the period just before\nthe mitral valve closes.",
