    "explanation": "Purkinje cells are the only output of the cerebellar\ncortex. Their output is always inhibitory, owing to the\nneurotransmitter released which is γ-aminobutyric acid\n(GABA).\nThis output projects to the deep cerebellar nuclei and the\nvestibular nucleus, and modulates the output of the\ncerebellum, regulating the rate, range, and direction of\nmovement.",
