    "explanation": "Dromotropic effects produce changes in conduction velocity,\nmostly in the AV node.\n• Negative dromotropic effects → decreased\nconduction velocity\n• Positive dromotropic effects → increased\nconduction velocity\n(Choice A) Contractility or inotropism is the intrinsic ability\nof cardiac muscle to develop force at a given muscle length.\n(Choice C) Chronotropic effects produce changes in\nthe heart rate, such that:\n• Negative chronotropic effect → decreased heart rate\n• Positive chronotropic effect → increased heart rate",
