    "explanation": "Type I skeletal muscle fiber characteristics:\n• Slow contraction velocity\n• Red fiber color\n• Oxidative phosphorylation is the predominant\nmetabolism\n• Rich in mitochondria and myoglobin\n• Supports endurance training\nType II skeletal muscle fiber characteristics:\n• Fast contraction velocity\n• White fiber color\n• Anaerobic glycolysis is the predominant metabolism\n• Low in mitochondria and myoglobin\n• Supports weight training and sprinting",
