    "explanation": "A sarcomere runs from Z line to Z line.\n(Choice B) Light bands, or I bands, are named for being\nisotropic to polarized light. They contain the thin filaments.\n(Choice C) Dark bands or A bands are anisotropic to light.\nThey contain the myosin filaments as well as the ends of actin\nfilaments where they overlap the myosin.\n(Choice D) T-tubules are an extensive tubular network that\ncarry depolarization from the sarcolemmal membrane to the\ncell interior.",
