    "id": "notion-physiology-0008",
    "subject": "physiology",
    "originalNumber": 8,
    "stem": "Which condition decreases insulin resistance?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Hypertriglyceridemia"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Increased FFA"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Weight reduction"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Obesity"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "C",
    "explanation": "Insulin resistance is part of a cascade of disorders that is often called metabolic syndrome which includes obesity, insulin resistance, fasting hyperglycemia, lipid abnormalities such as increased triglycerides, and hypertension.",
    "choiceRationales": {
      "A": "Hypertriglyceridemia, or elevated levels of triglycerides in the blood, is associated with insulin resistance. Elevated triglycerides are often observed in individuals with metabolic syndrome, a condition that includes insulin resistance as one of its components. Therefore, hypertriglyceridemia does not decrease insulin resistance; rather, it is often a marker of insulin resistance.",
      "B": "Increased levels of free fatty acids are associated with insulin resistance. Elevated FFAs can interfere with insulin signaling, contributing to decreased insulin sensitivity. In conditions such as obesity, there is often an increase in circulating free fatty acids, which can contribute to insulin resistance.",
      "C": "Insulin resistance is part of a cascade of disorders that is often called metabolic syndrome which includes obesity, insulin resistance, fasting hyperglycemia, lipid abnormalities such as increased triglycerides, and hypertension.",
      "D": "Obesity is a major contributor to insulin resistance. Adipose tissue in obese individuals releases pro-inflammatory substances and adipokines that can interfere with insulin signaling, leading to decreased insulin sensitivity. Addressing obesity through weight reduction is a strategy to improve insulin resistance."
    },
