    "explanation": "Immunity is the ability to resist almost all types of organisms or toxins that tend to damage the tissues and organs. Innate Immunity: Results from general processes, rather than from processes directed at specific disease organisms. Acquired immunity: Does not develop until after the body is first attacked by a bacterium, virus, or toxin; often weeks or months are required for the immunity to develop. The immune mechanism normally \"recognizes\" a person's own tissues as being distinctive from bacteria or viruses, and the person's immunity system forms few antibodies or activated T cells against his or her own antigens, hence the tolerance to autoimmune diseases. Hypersensitivity reaction is not part of immunity, rather, an undesirable effect of immunity. We have no innate tolerance for allergic reactions but some people do have allergic tendencies.",
