    "explanation": "T helper cells, specifically CD4-positive T cells, are the primary target of HIV. The virus infects and destroys these cells, leading to a decline in the immune system's ability to mount an effective response against infections. The loss of T helper cells is a hallmark of HIV infection and is a key factor in the progression to acquired immunodeficiency syndrome (AIDS).",
