    "subject": "physiology",
    "originalNumber": 46,
    "stem": "A 45 year old hypertensive, diabetic, smoker was rushed to the Emergency Room due to sudden dyspnea, diaphoresis, and pallor. Vital signs showed BP of 80/50, PR: 20 bpm, RR: 35, JVP: 6 cm at 45 degree angle. There were bibasal crackles, faint heart sounds, S3. Your ECG finding MOST significant to your diagnosis is:",
