    "correctChoice": "D",
    "explanation": "In a patient with hypercortisolism, if the etiology is a\npituitary secreting ACTH, the expected finding will be\nnot suppressed to low dose dexamethasone suppression\ntest but suppressed by high dose. If the tumor is a\ncortisol secreting tumor in the adrenal cortex, then it will\nnot be suppressed by both low and high dose\ndexamethasone.\nSource: Physiology by Linda Costanzo 3rd ed p413",
