    "explanation": "SIMILAR TO PREVIOUS BOARD EXAM\nCONCEPT/PRINCIPLE. Cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) is\nsimilar in composition to the interstitial fluid of the\nbrain. Therefore, it is similar to an ultrafiltrate of plasma\nand has a very low protein concentration because large\nprotein molecules cannot cross the blood–brain barrier.\nThere are other differences in composition between CSF\nand blood that are created by transporters in the choroid\nplexus, but the low protein concentration of CSF is the\nmost dramatic difference.",
