    "explanation": "Testosterone increases bone matrix and causes calcium\nretention. Because of the ability of testosterone to\nincrease the size and strength of bones, it is often used in\nolder men to treat osteoporosis. (Guyton). SIMILAR TO\nPREVIOUS BOARD EXAM CONCEPT.",
