    "explanation": "Aldosterone increases K+secretion. The mechanism\ninvolves increased sodium entry entry into the cells\nacross the luminal membrane and increased pumping of\nNa+ out of the cells by Na+-K+ pump. Stimulation of the\nNa+-K+ pump simultaneously increases K uptake into\nthe principal cellls, increasing the intracellular K+\nconcentration and driving force for K+ secretion.\nHypoaldosteronism decreses K\" secretion and causes\nhyperkalemia.",
