    "explanation": "the apices of the lung is zone 2, while the mid and basal\nlung regions are zone 3. Zone 2 states that only during\nsystole that there would be pulmonary perfusion since at\nthat time it will exceed the alveolar pressure. Zone 3\nmeans there is a continuous blood flow since the\nalveolar capillary pressure is always greater than\nalveolar pressure regardless on what phase of cardiac\ncycle. Zone 1 happens only if the patient is having severe\nblood loss or in a positive pressure ventilation.",
