    "explanation": "Pancreatic bicarbonate secretion into the small intestine\nis essential for neutralizationof gastric acid emptied into\nthe small intestine. Unlike the gastric mucosal lining, the\nsmall intestine does not have a significant endogenous\nmechanism. Upon delivery into the proximal small\nintestine, hydrogen ions stimulate release of secretin\nwhich stimulates pancreatic bicarbonate secretion. The\nacid ouput of the stomach during a meal is matched\nequallly by the pancreatic output of bicarbonate",
