    "stem": "A man presents with hypertension and hypokalemia.\nMeasurement of his arterial blood gases reveal a pH\nof 7.5 and a calculated HCO3 of 32 mEq/L. His serum\ncortisol and VMA are normal, his serum aldosterone\nis increased and his plasma renin activity is\ndecreased. Which of the following is the most likely\ncause of his hypertension?",
